**Independent delta review receipt — unedited. Delta `dafefe1..884c4c1` (supplier `befe794` + Design R-15 fold). Reviewer: fresh-context agent, model fable, read-only.** Text verbatim:

---

**Verdict: ACCEPT** (platform.ts hunk reported for Auth, not accepted here).

**A. PASS** — `git diff --stat dafefe1 884c4c1` = exactly `src/handlers/platform.ts` (+2/−1), `test/shared-link-browser.test.ts`, `test/synthetic-owner-auth.test.ts`, `ui/app.js`, `ui/shared-link.js`. No contract/migration/wrangler files touched.

**B. Report only** — `src/handlers/platform.ts:48-49`:
```ts
const changed = await ctx.db.prepare("UPDATE login_code SET redeemed_at = ? WHERE id = ? AND redeemed_at IS NULL").bind(Date.now(), row.id).run();
if (changed.meta.changes !== 1) throw new CapError("INVALID_PARAMS", "code_used", "codes are single-use; request a new one");
```
Under D1/SQLite semantics a single UPDATE statement is atomic; the `redeemed_at IS NULL` predicate plus `meta.changes === 1` makes exactly one caller win and mints a session only after winning (mintSession is at line 51, after the guard). The concurrent loser reaches the `code_used` path at line 49 (its pre-read at line 46 checks `row.used_at`, a different column, so the pre-check does not filter it; the guarded UPDATE does). Note for Auth: the line 46 pre-check reads `used_at` while the write sets `redeemed_at` — pre-existing, unchanged by this patch; the new guard makes it moot. Test `test/synthetic-owner-auth.test.ts:56-77` runs two overlapping consumes through real `execute` against Miniflare D1 and asserts 1 win, 1 INVALID_PARAMS, `COUNT(session)==1`.

**C. PASS** — `ui/shared-link.js:135-139`:
```js
try { receipt = await client.receipt(); } catch (error) {
  const kind = errorKind(error);
  return { state: kind === 'unavailable' ? 'unavailable' : kind === 'rateLimited' ? 'rateLimited' : 'transient' };
}
```
`errorKind` (`ui/shared-link.js:112-118`) maps 429/RATE_LIMITED → rateLimited, NOT_FOUND_OR_NOT_VISIBLE/NOT_AUTHENTICATED → unavailable, anything else → transient. A 429 or transport failure on the probe no longer yields `unavailable`. Submit path `ui/app.js:326` renders `sharedCopy.rateLimited`/`sharedCopy.transient` into `#participant-resume` for those states and only calls `showSharedUnavailable` for `unavailable`/`closed`.

**D. PASS** — `ui/app.js:375-380`:
```js
let receipt;
try { receipt = await state.shared.receipt(); }
catch (error) {
  if (token === null && entryFailureKind(error, true) === 'cannotResume') { showSharedUnavailable('cannotResume'); return; }
  throw error;
}
```
No-fragment path: `token === null`, stored bearer present (line 374 gate), one `GET /receipt`; NOT_AUTHENTICATED/NOT_FOUND → `cannotResume` → `showSharedUnavailable` (`ui/app.js:355-359`) writes `sharedCopy.cannotResume` into `#participant-error` and hides `#answers`/`#review`; early `return` means the outer catch (which would throw to `run()` and populate `#error`) is not reached. No POST (open() is skipped when token is null; no fresh open). Storage is not touched on this path (no `remove`/`set`). No restart/next control is rendered (`#recover` is set visible only after a successful receipt at line 381).

**E. PASS** — New cases: `test/synthetic-owner-auth.test.ts:56` real handler via `execute` + Miniflare D1; `test/shared-link-browser.test.ts:188` (resolveConflict kinds) module-level, stubbed `receipt()`; `:214` (R-15 real-API) real client against the worker with a counting fetch, asserts `err.code === 'NOT_AUTHENTICATED'`, `entryFailureKind(...) === 'cannotResume'`, `calls` toEqual `["GET /v2/participate/receipt"]`, storage before/after JSON identity (225-227); `:326` (R-15 fake-DOM boot) real worker via `boot(storage, "", countingFetch)`, asserts one GET, `#participant-error` with `copy.cannotResume`, `#error` hidden and not matching /NOT_AUTHENTICATED/, `#answers` hidden, storage byte-identical.

**F. PASS** — `npm run typecheck`: `tsc --noEmit` clean. `npx vitest run`: `Test Files 25 passed (25) / Tests 129 passed (129) / Duration 73.23s`.

**G. PASS** — The delta adds no new user-facing string; `copy` in `ui/shared-link.js` is unchanged by the diff. The three strings newly routed (`cannotResume`, `rateLimited`, `transient`) each have a verbatim row in `cookbook cos/c2-shared-link-copy:design-system/copy.md` (3/3).
